%Estimate Number of Parameters for LDA, QDA, NB
All methods estimate $K - 1$ class priors $\pik$ (as $\sum_{k=1}^K \pik = 1$) and $K$ class means $\muk \in \R^p$, i.e., $Kp$ parameters.
A symmetric $p \times p$ covariance matrix has $p$ variances and $(p^2 - p) / 2$ covariances, i.e., $p + (p^2 - p) / 2 = p(p + 1) / 2$ parameters.

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{LDA}, $\xv | y = k \sim \normal(\muk, \Sigma)$ with one covariance matrix shared by all classes:
  $$\underbrace{(K - 1)}_{\pik} + \underbrace{Kp}_{\muk} + \underbrace{\frac{p(p + 1)}{2}}_{\Sigma}$$

  \item \textbf{QDA}, $\xv | y = k \sim \normal(\muk, \Sigma_k)$ with one covariance matrix per class:
  $$\underbrace{(K - 1)}_{\pik} + \underbrace{Kp}_{\muk} + \underbrace{K \cdot \frac{p(p + 1)}{2}}_{\Sigma_k}$$

  \item \textbf{Gaussian NB}, features conditionally independent given the class, $x_j | y = k \sim \normal(\mu_{kj}, \sigma_{kj}^2)$ for $j = 1, \ldots, p$, i.e., diagonal $\Sigma_k = \diag(\sigma_{k1}^2, \ldots, \sigma_{kp}^2)$:
  $$\underbrace{(K - 1)}_{\pik} + \underbrace{Kp}_{\mu_{kj}} + \underbrace{Kp}_{\sigma_{kj}^2} = (K - 1) + 2Kp$$
\end{enumerate}
For comparison: (multinomial) logistic regression has $(K - 1)(p + 1)$ parameters, i.e., $p + 1$ for $K = 2$.
